WEBVTT

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:18.600
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:37.980
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:45.950
And takes me

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.900
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:58.050
To the home of wind

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.400
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:37.790
Anne and Diana had regained
their original way of life

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:42.070
and it was now a cold February.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:49.860
One, two, three, four,

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:50.980
five?

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.910
Oh, what could it be?

00:01:56.650 --> 00:02:00.130
Marilla, can I go over to see
Diana just for a minute?

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:01.610
Why?

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:07.030
Haven't you both talked in the snow
for over half an hour just now?

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:12.380
But she wants to see me!
She has something very important to tell me.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:14.910
How do you know she has?

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:16.520
She just signaled to me.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:22.440
We have arranged a way to signal
with our candles and cardboard.

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:27.500
You'll be setting fire to the curtains
with your signaling nonsense.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.160
Oh, we're very careful, Marilla.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:37.500
Diana just send a signal of that she
has something important to reveal,

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.120
and I'm really suffering to know what it is.

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:43.770
Well, you needn't suffer any longer.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:45.010
You can go.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.410
But you're to be back here in
just ten minutes, remember that.

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:51.450
Alright.

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:53.560
Close the door!

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:16.680
Oh, Marilla, what do you think?

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.270
You know tomorrow is Diana's birthday.

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:24.320
Well, her mother told her she could
ask me to go home with her from school,

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:26.950
and stay all night with her.

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:34.530
Her cousins are coming over from Newbridge
to go to the Debating Club concert

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:38.520
at the hall tomorrow night. And they are
going to take Diana and me to the concert.

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:43.040
If you'll let me go, that is.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:47.230
You will, won't you, Marilla?

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:51.080
Oh, I feel so excited.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:54.480
You can calm down then,
because you're not going.

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:59.200
That club concert, it's all nonsense.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:03.960
And little girls should not be
allowed to go out to such places at all.

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:07.830
Oh, I'm sure the Debating
Club is a most respectable affair.

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:10.450
I'm not saying it isn't.

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:13.880
But you're not going to begin
gadding about to concerts

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:17.640
and staying out all hours of the night.

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:23.360
I'm surprised at
Mrs. Barry's letting Diana go.

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:26.780
But it's such a very special occasion,

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:32.900
Diana has only one birthday in a year.
It isn't as if birthdays were common things.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:37.780
And the minister is going to take part,
he's going to give an address.

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:39.460
That will be the same thing as a sermon.

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:43.320
Please, mayn't I go, Marilla?

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:48.290
You heard what I said, didn't you?
Take off your boots now and go to bed.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:51.090
It's past eight.

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:04.530
There's just one more thing, Marilla.

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:09.430
Mrs. Barry told that we
might sleep in the spare-room bed.

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:15.710
Think of the honor of your little
Anne being put in the spare-room bed.

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:17.920
It's an honor you'll have to get along without.

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:19.620
Go to bed, Anne.

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:22.370
And don't let me
hear another word out of you.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:42.670
Well now, Marilla,
I think you ought to let Anne go.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.750
I don't then.

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:47.670
Who's bringing this child up, Matthew?

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:50.410
You or me?

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:54.280
Well now, you.

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:56.910
Don't interfere then.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:59.250
Well now...

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:07.510
I ain't interfering. It ain't
interfering to have your own opinion.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:13.710
And my opinion is that
you ought to let Anne go.

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:19.770
You'd think I ought to let Anne
go to the moon if she took the notion.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:22.320
I might have let her spend the
night with Diana,

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:24.290
but I don't approve of this concert plan.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.040
She'd go there and catch cold like as not,

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:31.370
and have her head filled up
with nonsense and excitement.

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:34.430
It would unsettle her for a week.

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:38.110
I understand that child's disposition

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:41.140
and  what's good
for it better than you, Matthew.

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:46.600
I think you ought to let Anne go.

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:09.970
Why are you taking so long, Anne?

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:11.980
If you don't hurry you'll be late to School.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:28.470
I think you ought to let Anne go.

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:32.820
Very well, she can go,

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:35.880
since nothing else'll please you.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:44.710
Oh, Marilla, say those blessed words again.

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:47.200
I guess once is enough to say them.

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:49.250
This is Matthew's doings and I
wash my hands of it.

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:54.000
If you catch pneumonia
sleeping in a strange bed

00:07:54.000 --> 00:08:00.050
or coming out of that hot hall in
the middle of the night, don't blame me!

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:02.240
Blame Matthew.

00:08:02.510 --> 00:08:04.100
Thank you, Marilla!

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:08.470
My heart was just set on going to
that concert.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.580
I never was to a concert in my life,

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:18.330
and when the other girls talk about
them in school I feel so out of it.

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:20.080
Oh, Marilla...

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:22.910
Matthew knew just how I felt about it.

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:26.760
He understands me,
and it's so nice to be understood, Marilla.

00:08:27.350 --> 00:08:30.060
I never agreed,
so don't go thinking I understand.

00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:34.400
Don't be like this,
your hands are still wet.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:46.780
I've been waiting at the brook so long.

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:51.510
I was wandering if something had happened.
You made me worried.

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:58.500
I forgot to ask the ten cents
for the concert fee from Marilla.

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:01.870
I remembered
suddenly and went back to get it.

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:04.040
Then Marilla permitted you to go?

00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:05.080
Yes.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:32.750
Anne was too excited about the concert,
so she couldn't concentrate in the lessons.

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:35.950
Gilbert spelled her down in class

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:38.710
and left her clear
out of sight in mental arithmetic.

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:41.010
However in view of the concert

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:44.280
and the spare-room bed,
her humiliation was bearable.

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:56.640
For Anne the real excitement began
with the dismissal of school.

00:10:06.510 --> 00:10:13.500
The tea that Mrs. Barry prepared was
perfect for Diana's birthday.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:21.440
Then they experimented with at least half a
dozen different ways of arranging their hair

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:24.960
but in the end they decided
to go with their original.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:31.200
Anne could not help a little pang at
her plain black tam and shapeless,

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:34.320
tight-sleeved, homemade gray-cloth.

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:38.590
But she remembered she
had an imagination and could use it.

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:06.300
My cousins are here.

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:14.820
Welcome!

00:11:15.590 --> 00:11:17.000
Hello, Diana!

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.000
Hello!

00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:20.370
Tommy, good evening!

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:22.930
Good evening!

00:11:55.090 --> 00:11:59.450
Anne and Diana,
enjoyed their trip to the club.

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:02.130
The program that night

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:07.130
was a series of "thrills"
for at least one listener in the audience.

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:24.220
The carnations on Prissy's head are real.

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:25.220
No way?

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:29.640
Master Philips bought them
from town personally for her.

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:30.800
Really?

00:12:32.990 --> 00:12:38.150
I climbed the slimy ladder.
dark, without one ray of light...

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:45.830
Anne shivered in luxurious
sympathy by prissy's recital.

00:12:46.130 --> 00:12:49.170
When the choir sang, Anne listened
as if the room was full of angels,

00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:51.140
and laughed when Sam Sloane

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:55.860
proceeded to explain and
illustrate "How Sockery Set a Hen".

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:10.710
I come to bury Caesar,

00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:14.250
not to praise him.

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:17.550
The evil that men do lives after them.

00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:24.800
The noble Brutus
hath told you Caesar was ambitious.

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:29.800
For Brutus is an honourable man.

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:34.120
Mr. Phillips gave Mark Antony's oration

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:38.140
over the dead body of Caesar in
the most heart-stirring tones,

00:13:38.140 --> 00:13:41.900
looking at Prissy at the end of every sentence.

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:47.090
Anne forgot everything he did
to her and applauded to him.

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:51.550
My heart is in the coffin there with Caesar.

00:13:56.150 --> 00:14:00.570
Only one number on the program
failed to interest her.

00:14:12.190 --> 00:14:17.300
A soldier of the Legion from
Bingen lay dying in Algiers.

00:14:17.300 --> 00:14:21.980
The dying soldier said to a comrade:

00:14:21.980 --> 00:14:24.210
"Take a message to some distant people."

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:27.450
"One of them is my dear sister."

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:37.300
"There's another, -- not a sister."

00:14:37.300 --> 00:14:41.590
"in the happy days gone by,
you'd have known her by..."

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:45.750
Besides that number,

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:48.720
Anne thoroughly enjoyed herself that night.

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:55.340
They talked constantly
about it after the concert ended.

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:04.860
It was eleven when they arrived
at Orchard Slope, sated with dissipation.

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:10.160
Everybody seemed asleep
and the house was dark and silent.

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:16.250
Oh, Anne, how could you
pretend not to listen to Gil?

00:15:16.580 --> 00:15:19.360
When he came to the line,
"THERE'S ANOTHER, not A SISTER,

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:23.000
he looked right down at you.

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:26.460
Diana, you are my bosom friend,

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:30.630
but I cannot allow even you to
speak to me of that person.

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:35.820
Let's run a race and see
who'll get to the bed first.

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:37.010
All right!

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:38.670
Ready... Go!

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:47.520
Merciful goodness!

00:16:00.170 --> 00:16:02.410
Oh, who was it... What was it?

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:06.710
It was Aunt Josephine.
I don't know why she was there.

00:16:06.710 --> 00:16:09.160
But I know she will be furious.

00:16:09.160 --> 00:16:10.860
It's dreadful,

00:16:11.260 --> 00:16:14.350
but did you ever know
anything so funny, Anne?

00:16:14.590 --> 00:16:16.630
Who is your Aunt Josephine?

00:16:16.820 --> 00:16:19.650
She's father's aunt
and she lives in Charlottetown.

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:21.660
She's awfully old,

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:25.250
and I don't believe
she was EVER a little girl.

00:16:25.770 --> 00:16:29.350
We were expecting her out for a visit,
but not so soon.

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:33.680
She's awfully prim and proper
and she'll scold dreadfully about this.

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:38.760
Well, we'll have to sleep with Minnie May
and you can't think how she kicks.

00:17:01.350 --> 00:17:06.620
Miss Josephine Barry did not appear at
the early breakfast the next morning.

00:17:07.890 --> 00:17:12.760
Diana preserved a discreet silence

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:17.510
so nothing happened
until Anne returned to Green Gables.

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:21.560
Diana! Diana!

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:22.560
Yes!

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:31.790
Diana, did you really
jump onto your aunt yesterday?

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:36.720
I've told you already,
you don't have to listen to her.

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:42.770
And I won't be staying here.

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:46.200
I shall return home tomorrow.

00:17:46.340 --> 00:17:48.960
Aunt, please reconsider.

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:51.130
No. I will be going.

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:55.420
I've already packed up
and can move away anytime.

00:17:56.300 --> 00:17:59.190
And about your child's music fees.

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:02.680
I suppose you should forget about them,

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:06.940
I will have nothing to do with such a tomboy.

00:18:06.940 --> 00:18:11.230
A person like her has
no right to take music lessons.

00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:17.320
Diana, apologize to your aunt right now!

00:18:18.100 --> 00:18:22.360
That's useless!
I don't want to talk with her at all!

00:18:23.210 --> 00:18:25.090
Aunt, I am very sorry.

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:35.560
Anne was in blissful ignorance of the
disturbance resulted in the Barry household

00:18:35.570 --> 00:18:39.640
until the late afternoon, when she went
down to Mrs. Lynde's on an errand for Marilla.

00:18:41.210 --> 00:18:46.370
Anne would not allow her
best friend to get into trouble

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:48.630
for something she suggested.

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:53.820
When she left Mrs. Lynde's she took her way
across the crusted fields to Orchard Slope.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:05.670
I Heard that your Aunt Josephine
was very cross about it, wasn't she?

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:07.020
Yes.

00:19:08.400 --> 00:19:11.820
She was fairly dancing with rage.

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:16.790
She says she won't
stay and I'm sure I don't care.

00:19:17.600 --> 00:19:20.090
But Father and Mother do.

00:19:21.030 --> 00:19:23.620
Why didn't you tell them it was my fault?

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:26.260
It's likely I'd do such a thing, isn't it?

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:31.030
I'm no telltale, and anyhow
I was just as much to blame as you.

00:19:31.030 --> 00:19:33.350
Well, I'm going in to tell her myself.

00:19:33.670 --> 00:19:35.610
Anne Shirley, you'd never!

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:44.740
Why, she'll eat you alive!

00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:47.570
Don't frighten me
any more than I am frightened.

00:19:47.850 --> 00:19:51.330
I'd rather walk up to a cannon's mouth.

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:54.060
But I've got to do it, Diana.

00:19:54.140 --> 00:19:57.500
It was my fault and I've got to confess.

00:19:57.870 --> 00:20:00.650
I've had practice in confessing, fortunately.

00:20:02.270 --> 00:20:03.150
Anne!

00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:08.000
Come in.

00:20:16.120 --> 00:20:17.770
Miss Josephine Barry.

00:20:20.330 --> 00:20:21.850
Who are you?

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:26.490
I'm Anne of Green Gables,
and I've come to confess, if you please.

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:29.510
Confess what?

00:20:30.100 --> 00:20:35.200
That it was my fault about jumping into
bed on you last night. I suggested it.

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:38.630
Diana would never have thought of such a thing.

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:42.450
Diana is a very ladylike girl, Miss Barry.

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:47.030
So you must see how unjust it is to blame her.

00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:49.560
Oh, I must, hey?

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:52.980
But Diana did her share of the jumping at least.

00:20:53.030 --> 00:20:56.620
Such carryings on in a respectable house!

00:20:56.870 --> 00:20:59.450
But we were only in fun.

00:20:59.460 --> 00:21:04.890
I think you ought to forgive us now that
we've apologized, Miss Josephine Barry.

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:11.100
And anyhow, please forgive Diana
and let her have her music lessons.

00:21:11.310 --> 00:21:15.150
Diana's heart is set on her
music lessons, Miss Barry,

00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:20.210
and I know too well what it is to set your
heart on a thing and not get it.

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:23.910
If you must be cross with anyone,
be cross with me.

00:21:23.960 --> 00:21:29.410
I've been so used to having people cross at me
that I can endure it much better than Diana.

00:21:44.160 --> 00:21:48.170
And what were you doing in the spare room?

00:21:49.630 --> 00:21:56.440
Well, I dare say your claim to sympathy
is just as strong as mine.

00:21:57.740 --> 00:22:01.070
It all depends on the way we look at it.

00:22:04.770 --> 00:22:08.330
Sit down here and tell me about yourself.

00:22:08.600 --> 00:22:10.960
I am very sorry I can't.

00:22:11.900 --> 00:22:14.760
It is my duty to
go home to Miss Marilla Cuthbert.

00:22:15.150 --> 00:22:20.800
Miss Marilla Cuthbert is a very kind
lady who has taken me to bring up properly.

00:22:20.800 --> 00:22:24.910
She is doing her best, but
it is very discouraging work.

00:22:25.270 --> 00:22:29.090
You must not blame
her because I jumped on the bed.

00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:32.620
But before I go I do wish you
would tell me if you will forgive Diana

00:22:32.620 --> 00:22:37.510
and stay just as
long as you meant to in Avonlea.

00:22:38.800 --> 00:22:44.120
I think perhaps I will if you
will come over and talk to me occasionally.

00:22:46.220 --> 00:22:48.140
So you have forgiven us?

00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:50.850
I suppose.

00:22:52.050 --> 00:22:53.030
Diana!

00:22:58.200 --> 00:23:00.910
My, my, that was fast.

00:23:02.840 --> 00:23:08.260
That evening Miss Barry
gave Diana a silver bangle bracelet,

00:23:08.600 --> 00:23:12.610
unpacked her valise once again,

00:23:13.170 --> 00:23:15.210
and said...

00:23:15.890 --> 00:23:18.910
I've made up my mind
to stay simply for the sake of

00:23:18.910 --> 00:23:20.790
getting better
acquainted with that Anne-girl.

00:23:20.900 --> 00:23:25.970
And Marilla's only comment to
Matthew when she heard the story was...

00:23:26.490 --> 00:23:28.740
I told you so.

00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:30.190
That was all.

00:23:31.120 --> 00:23:36.160
Miss Josephine Barry
stayed her month out and over.

00:23:36.450 --> 00:23:41.080
She was a more agreeable guest than
usual, for Anne kept her in good humor.

00:23:43.800 --> 00:23:46.740
When Miss Barry went away she said:

00:23:46.850 --> 00:23:51.020
Remember, you Anne-girl, when
you come to town you're to visit me

00:23:51.140 --> 00:23:54.420
and I'll put you in my very
sparest spare-room bed to sleep.

00:23:58.420 --> 00:24:02.900
Anne had met another kindred spirit.

00:24:18.220 --> 00:24:19.500
In the coming Spring,

00:24:19.950 --> 00:24:23.610
Anne remembered her
first days in Green Gables.

